/*
  MotorSection.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0293 · MotorSection (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `MotorSection` resolves (table "MotorSection") lives here with its web
  `t(key, default)` English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  The first group is the exact set of keys extracted from the web source
  (features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/MotorSection.tsx — the "Powertrain" title,
  the eight MetricCard labels, and the empty message), reusing the web
  `vehicles.detail.*` namespace verbatim. The second group backs the native chrome (the
  P4 leaf freshness / loading / error copy) so the Swift sources hold no English prose
  literals. The unit suffixes ("V" / "A" / "Nm") and the temperature symbols ("°C" / "°F")
  are device/data literals carried in code, not translated strings (matching the web,
  where they are template literals, not `t()` calls).
*/

